      "html": "<style>\n/* ── Course Module: visual identity overrides ── */\n.d-pastel-card {\n  --bg: #fbfaf6; --bg-soft: #f4f1e8; --surface: #ffffff; --surface-2: #f6f3ea;\n  --text-1: #2a2418; --text-2: #5a5140; --text-3: #8a7f68;\n  --accent: #2d7d6e; --accent-2: #d88a3a; --accent-3: #c4593f;\n  --grad: linear-gradient(135deg, #2d7d6e, #4ea893);\n  --font-display: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, 'Noto Serif SC', serif;\n}\n\n/* ── Course Module custom elements (sidebar, objectives, MCQ, exercise) ── */\n\n.cm-sidebar-slide { display: grid !important; grid-template-columns: 14cqi 1fr; gap: 3cqi; align-content: start !important; justify-content: unset !important; }\n.cm-full-slide { display: flex !important; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center !important; }\n\n.cm-sidebar { border-right: 1px solid var(--border); padding-right: 2cqi; }\n.cm-sidebar-brand { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.6cqi; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }\n.cm-sidebar-brand::before { content: \"✦ \"; color: var(--accent-2); }\n.cm-sidebar h5 { font-size: 0.7cqi; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--text-3); margin: 2cqi 0 0.8cqi; }\n.cm-sidebar h5:first-of-type { margin-top: 2.5cqi; }\n\n.cm-obj-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; font-size: 0.75cqi; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.5; }\n.cm-obj-list li { padding: 0.5cqi 0 0.5cqi 1.4cqi; position: relative; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--border); }\n.cm-obj-list li::before { content: \"○\"; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.5cqi; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.7cqi; }\n.cm-obj-list li.done { color: var(--text-3); }\n.cm-obj-list li.done::before { content: \"●\"; color: var(--accent-3); }\n.cm-obj-list li.current { color: var(--text-1); font-weight: 700; }\n.cm-obj-list li.current::before { content: \"▸\"; color: var(--accent-2); font-size: 0.75cqi; top: 0.45cqi; }\n\n.cm-main { min-width: 0; }\n\n.cm-concept-box { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.4cqi 1.6cqi; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }\n.cm-concept-box h4 { color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 0.4cqi; font-size: 1.3cqi; font-weight: 700; }\n.cm-concept-box p { margin: 0; }\n\n.cm-pill { display: inline-block; padding: 0.15cqi 0.6cqi; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.7cqi; color: var(--text-2); font-family: var(--font-mono, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace); }\n\n.cm-exercise { background: #fff8ed; border: 1.5px dashed var(--accent-2); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.4cqi 1.6cqi; }\n.cm-exercise::before { content: \"✎ Exercise\"; display: block; font-size: 0.65cqi; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--accent-2); margin-bottom: 0.6cqi; text-transform: uppercase; }\n.cm-exercise ol { color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0.6cqi 0 0; padding-left: 1.3cqi; font-size: 0.95cqi; }\n.cm-exercise ol li { margin-bottom: 0.2cqi; }\n\n.cm-mcq { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1cqi 1.3cqi; margin-bottom: 0.6cqi; display: flex; gap: 0.8cqi; align-items: flex-start; }\n.cm-mcq-letter { flex: none; width: 1.6cqi; height: 1.6cqi; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--text-3); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.75cqi; color: var(--text-2); }\n.cm-mcq.correct { border-color: var(--accent-3); background: rgba(46,157,112,.08); }\n.cm-mcq.correct .cm-mcq-letter { border-color: var(--accent-3); background: var(--accent-3); color: #fff; }\n\n.cm-codebox { background: #2a2340; color: #fef8f1; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.9cqi 1.2cqi; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75cqi; line-height: 1.75; overflow: auto; margin-top: 1cqi; }\n.cm-codebox .cmt { color: #9089a8; font-style: italic; }\n.cm-codebox .kw { color: #e8a770; }\n.cm-codebox .str { color: #8ec6b2; }\n\n.cm-lede { font-size: 1.1cqi; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 62ch; }\n.cm-h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 4cqi; line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--text-1); margin: 0 0 1cqi; }\n.cm-h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }\n.cm-h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2.8cqi; line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--text-1); margin: 0 0 0.8cqi; }\n.cm-h2 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }\n\n.cm-callout { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-2); background: var(--surface-2); padding: 0.9cqi 1.2cqi; border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0; margin-top: 1cqi; font-size: 0.85cqi; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-2); }\n.cm-callout b { color: var(--accent-2); }\n\n.cm-dim { color: var(--text-3); }\n.cm-spacer-sm { height: 0.5cqi; }\n.cm-spacer { height: 1cqi; }\n.cm-spacer-lg { height: 1.8cqi; }\n\n.cm-footer { color: var(--text-3); font-size: 0.7cqi; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: auto; padding-top: 1cqi; }\n\n/* Override pastel-card chr-kicker to be cqi-based for 16:9 */\n.cm-kicker { color: var(--accent-2); font-size: 0.7cqi; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-family: var(--font-sans); margin-bottom: 0.6cqi; }\n</style>\n<section class=\"slide cm-full-slide is-active\" data-title=\"Cover\">\n  <p class=\"cm-kicker\">CS 101 · MODULE 04</p>\n  <h1 class=\"cm-h1\">Recursion: solving<br>problems by <em>calling yourself</em>.</h1>\n  <p class=\"cm-lede\" style=\"max-width:62ch;margin-top:1.2cqi\">In this module you'll learn why a function that calls itself is not a trick, but the most natural way to describe problems that contain smaller copies of themselves.</p>\n  <div class=\"c-badge-row\" style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi;gap:0.6cqi\">\n    <span class=\"c-badge\">~ 45 min read</span>\n    <span class=\"c-badge\">prereq · functions, if/else</span>\n    <span class=\"c-badge\">lang · Python</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cm-footer\" style=\"margin-top:1.8cqi\"><span>Dr. A. Rivera · Spring 2026</span><span>1 / 7</span></div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<section class=\"slide cm-sidebar-slide\" data-title=\"Objectives\">\n  <aside class=\"cm-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"cm-sidebar-brand\">CS 101 · M04</div>\n    <h5>Learning objectives</h5>\n    <ul class=\"cm-obj-list\">\n      <li class=\"current\">Define recursion</li>\n      <li>Identify a base case</li>\n      <li>Trace a recursive call</li>\n      <li>Convert loop &harr; recursion</li>\n      <li>Recognize when recursion helps</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h5>Module progress</h5>\n    <p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.72cqi\">Page 2 of 7 · ~5 min in</p>\n  </aside>\n  <div class=\"cm-main\">\n    <p class=\"cm-kicker\">OBJECTIVES</p>\n    <h2 class=\"cm-h2\">By the end, you will be able to&hellip;</h2>\n    <div class=\"c-stack\" style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi\">\n      <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>① Explain recursion in one sentence.</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">\"A function that solves a problem by calling itself on a smaller version of that problem.\"</p></div>\n      <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>② Write a base case that always terminates.</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">Every recursive function must have an exit door, or it runs forever.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>③ Trace a call stack on paper.</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">Given <code>fact(4)</code>, draw the stack frames top-to-bottom.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>④ Convert a while-loop to a recursive equivalent.</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">And explain when one is clearer than the other.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<section class=\"slide cm-sidebar-slide\" data-title=\"Concept\">\n  <aside class=\"cm-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"cm-sidebar-brand\">CS 101 · M04</div>\n    <h5>Learning objectives</h5>\n    <ul class=\"cm-obj-list\">\n      <li class=\"done\">Define recursion</li>\n      <li class=\"current\">Identify a base case</li>\n      <li>Trace a recursive call</li>\n      <li>Convert loop &harr; recursion</li>\n      <li>Recognize when recursion helps</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h5>Key terms</h5>\n    <p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.72cqi\">base case · recursive case · call stack · tail call</p>\n  </aside>\n  <div class=\"cm-main\">\n    <p class=\"cm-kicker\">CORE CONCEPT</p>\n    <h2 class=\"cm-h2\">Two parts, always.</h2>\n    <p class=\"cm-lede\" style=\"margin-top:0.8cqi\">A recursive function has exactly two things inside it: a <b>base case</b> (when to stop) and a <b>recursive case</b> (how to shrink the problem before calling yourself).</p>\n    <div class=\"cm-callout\">\n      <b>Rule of thumb.</b> If you can't name the base case out loud, don't write the recursion yet. Draw it on paper first.\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"c-grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi\">\n      <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>Base case</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">The smallest possible input &mdash; one the function answers directly, without calling itself.</p><p style=\"margin-top:0.6cqi\"><span class=\"cm-pill\">e.g. <b>n == 0</b></span></p></div>\n      <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>Recursive case</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">Every other input &mdash; delegate to a smaller version of the same problem.</p><p style=\"margin-top:0.6cqi\"><span class=\"cm-pill\">e.g. <b>n × fact(n-1)</b></span></p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<section class=\"slide cm-sidebar-slide\" data-title=\"Example\">\n  <aside class=\"cm-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"cm-sidebar-brand\">CS 101 · M04</div>\n    <h5>Learning objectives</h5>\n    <ul class=\"cm-obj-list\">\n      <li class=\"done\">Define recursion</li>\n      <li class=\"done\">Identify a base case</li>\n      <li class=\"current\">Trace a recursive call</li>\n      <li>Convert loop &harr; recursion</li>\n      <li>Recognize when recursion helps</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h5>Try it yourself</h5>\n    <p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.72cqi\">Open repl.it and run the code on the right. Then try <code>fact(10)</code>.</p>\n  </aside>\n  <div class=\"cm-main\">\n    <p class=\"cm-kicker\">WORKED EXAMPLE</p>\n    <h2 class=\"cm-h2\">Factorial, 7 lines.</h2>\n    <div class=\"cm-codebox\"><pre style=\"margin:0\"><span class=\"cmt\"># fact(n) = n × (n-1) × … × 1,  and fact(0) = 1</span>\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> fact(n):\n    <span class=\"kw\">if</span> n == <span class=\"str\">0</span>:          <span class=\"cmt\"># base case</span>\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">1</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> n * fact(n - <span class=\"str\">1</span>)   <span class=\"cmt\"># recursive case</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">print</span>(fact(<span class=\"str\">4</span>))   <span class=\"cmt\"># → 24</span></pre></div>\n    <div class=\"cm-callout\">\n      <b>Trace fact(4).</b> 4 × fact(3) → 4 × (3 × fact(2)) → 4 × 3 × (2 × fact(1)) → 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 × fact(0) → 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 × 1 = <b>24</b>.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<section class=\"slide cm-sidebar-slide\" data-title=\"Exercise\">\n  <aside class=\"cm-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"cm-sidebar-brand\">CS 101 · M04</div>\n    <h5>Learning objectives</h5>\n    <ul class=\"cm-obj-list\">\n      <li class=\"done\">Define recursion</li>\n      <li class=\"done\">Identify a base case</li>\n      <li class=\"done\">Trace a recursive call</li>\n      <li class=\"current\">Convert loop &harr; recursion</li>\n      <li>Recognize when recursion helps</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h5>Time</h5>\n    <p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.72cqi\">~10 minutes · solo</p>\n  </aside>\n  <div class=\"cm-main\">\n    <p class=\"cm-kicker\">EXERCISE 4.1</p>\n    <h2 class=\"cm-h2\">Write <em>sum_to(n)</em>.</h2>\n    <p class=\"cm-lede\" style=\"margin-top:0.8cqi\">Return <code>1 + 2 + &hellip; + n</code> using recursion &mdash; no loops allowed.</p>\n    <div class=\"cm-exercise\" style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi\">\n      <p style=\"margin:0;font-size:1cqi;color:var(--text-1);font-weight:700\">Your task</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Write the base case. What does <code>sum_to(0)</code> return?</li>\n        <li>Write the recursive case in terms of <code>sum_to(n - 1)</code>.</li>\n        <li>Test it: <code>sum_to(5) == 15</code>, <code>sum_to(10) == 55</code>.</li>\n        <li>Bonus: what happens if you call <code>sum_to(-3)</code>? Fix it.</li>\n      </ol>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"margin-top:0.8cqi;font-size:0.78cqi\">Stuck? Remember: a base case is the smallest input you already know the answer to.</p>\n  </div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<section class=\"slide cm-sidebar-slide\" data-title=\"Check\">\n  <aside class=\"cm-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"cm-sidebar-brand\">CS 101 · M04</div>\n    <h5>Learning objectives</h5>\n    <ul class=\"cm-obj-list\">\n      <li class=\"done\">Define recursion</li>\n      <li class=\"done\">Identify a base case</li>\n      <li class=\"done\">Trace a recursive call</li>\n      <li class=\"done\">Convert loop &harr; recursion</li>\n      <li class=\"current\">Recognize when recursion helps</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h5>Self-assess</h5>\n    <p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.72cqi\">You should get 3/3.</p>\n  </aside>\n  <div class=\"cm-main\">\n    <p class=\"cm-kicker\">CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING</p>\n    <h2 class=\"cm-h2\">Which function will recurse forever?</h2>\n    <div style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi\">\n      <div class=\"cm-mcq\"><div class=\"cm-mcq-letter\">A</div><div><b style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">def f(n): return 1 if n == 0 else n * f(n - 1)</b><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.7cqi;margin:0.25cqi 0 0\">Base case <code>n == 0</code>, shrinks toward it. Terminates.</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"cm-mcq correct\"><div class=\"cm-mcq-letter\">B</div><div><b style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">def f(n): return n + f(n + 1)</b><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.7cqi;margin:0.25cqi 0 0\"><b style=\"color:var(--accent-3)\">✓ Correct.</b> No base case, and <code>n</code> grows &mdash; infinite recursion.</p></div></div>\n      <div class=\"cm-mcq\"><div class=\"cm-mcq-letter\">C</div><div><b style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">def f(n): return n if n &lt; 2 else f(n - 1) + f(n - 2)</b><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.7cqi;margin:0.25cqi 0 0\">Classic Fibonacci. Base case on <code>n &lt; 2</code>. Terminates.</p></div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<section class=\"slide cm-full-slide\" data-title=\"Summary\">\n  <p class=\"cm-kicker\">SUMMARY · MODULE 04</p>\n  <h1 class=\"cm-h1\">You can now&hellip;</h1>\n  <div class=\"c-grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi\">\n    <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>✓ Define recursion</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">A function that calls itself on a smaller input.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>✓ Write a safe base case</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">Every recursion needs an exit door.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>✓ Trace a call stack</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">You can unwind <code>fact(4)</code> by hand.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"cm-concept-box\"><h4>✓ Judge when to use it</h4><p class=\"cm-dim\" style=\"font-size:0.85cqi\">Trees and self-similar problems → recursion. Flat iteration → loop.</p></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cm-callout\" style=\"margin-top:1.2cqi\">\n    <b>Up next · Module 05.</b> Divide &amp; conquer: merge sort. We'll use everything you just learned &mdash; but on lists, not numbers.\n  </div>\n</section>"
    }
